From: Gustavo Foletto Mora <gusfmora@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 16:20:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] soc: qcom: mdt_loader: allocate MPD segment buffers with GFP_KERNEL

mdt_load_split_segment_dma() allocates the bounce buffer for each user-PD
segment with dma_alloc_coherent(..., GFP_DMA). GFP_DMA on its own carries
no __GFP_DIRECT_RECLAIM, so gfpflags_allow_blocking() is false and the DMA
layer treats the call as atomic: on a non-coherent arm64 platform with
DMA_DIRECT_REMAP it is served from the atomic coherent pool instead of the
page allocator. The function is nothing like atomic -- it runs from
rproc_boot() in the ath11k probe path and calls request_firmware() for the
same segment a few lines later.

The segments are hundreds of KB (268164 and 373700 bytes for the two Q6
user PDs on IPQ5018), so this only works when coherent_pool= on the
command line is large enough to hold them, which is why every ipq50xx
board passes coherent_pool=2M. With the default pool it fails:

    WARNING: CPU: 0 PID: 2734 at kernel/dma/pool.c:282 dma_alloc_from_pool+0x1e0/0x1ec
    ...
     dma_alloc_attrs+0x84/0xc4
     __qcom_mdt_load+0x2e8/0x494
     qcom_mdt_load_pd_seg+0x34/0x50
     wcss_pd_load+0x64/0x80
     rproc_start+0x30/0x168
     rproc_boot+0x4a0/0x4c0
     ath11k_ahb_power_up+0x24/0x64 [ath11k_ahb]
    qcom-q6-mpd pd-1: Error in dma alloc ptr: 268164
    remoteproc remoteproc1: Failed to load program segments: -12
    ath11k c000000.wifi: failed to boot the remote processor Q6

Use GFP_KERNEL. The DMA API picks the zone from the device's coherent
mask, so the GFP_DMA hint was redundant as well as harmful; the same
change is applied to the small args buffer next to it.

On a 256 MiB board this is worth 6-7 MiB of RAM: coherent_pool=2M
creates three 2 MiB pools and the one in use doubles itself on first
use, so the workaround was parking 8 MiB to hand out ~640 KB once at
boot.

Signed-off-by: Gustavo Foletto Mora <gusfmora@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/soc/qcom/mdt_loader.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/soc/qcom/mdt_loader.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/qcom/mdt_loader.c
@@ -122,7 +122,7 @@ static int mdt_load_split_segment_dma(int pas_id, unsigned int segment,
 	dma_addr_t dma_args, dma_addrs, dma_ptr;
 	int ret;
 
-	args = dma_alloc_coherent(dev, sizeof(*args) + sizeof(*addrs), &dma_args, GFP_DMA);
+	args = dma_alloc_coherent(dev, sizeof(*args) + sizeof(*addrs), &dma_args, GFP_KERNEL);
 	if (!args) {
 		dev_err(dev, "Error in dma alloc regin: %ld\n", sizeof(*args));
 		return -ENOMEM;
@@ -131,7 +131,7 @@ static int mdt_load_split_segment_dma(int pas_id, unsigned int segment,
 	addrs = (void *) args + sizeof(*args);
 	dma_addrs = dma_args + sizeof(*args);
 
-	ptr = dma_alloc_coherent(dev, phdr->p_filesz, &dma_ptr, GFP_DMA);
+	ptr = dma_alloc_coherent(dev, phdr->p_filesz, &dma_ptr, GFP_KERNEL);
 	if (!ptr) {
 		dev_err(dev, "Error in dma alloc ptr: %d\n", phdr->p_filesz);
 		return -ENOMEM;
